From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] lumaui: Apps › one permission page for every app format

ADR-052 step 3 (design-center 8bd4ccf, mockups/app-perms/settings.html).
A new adapter, "appperm", reads org.projectluma.AppPermissions1
(luma-application-installer, D-Bus activated) on the session bus: Apps and
AllFilesApps with GetAll, again on PropertiesChanged, Changed and Used, and an
app's GetApp when its page opens. It publishes CFAPPPERM and one bound key
per app and field (apperm_level, _net, _bg, _auto, _files, _dev_<kind>);
writes call SetFileLevel, SetNetwork, SetBackground, SetAutostart and
SetDevice. "appPerm" adds or removes a folder (SetFolder), reads a detail,
or removes the app (MoveStrayDocuments when asked, then luma-appctl remove
or flatpak uninstall, a failure reported). Without the service CFAPPPERM is null and an app's
page keeps its older rows.

An app's page, whatever its format, top to bottom: the name with "Version
· size with its data"; the hero with the origin ("Flatpak · from Flathub",
"Debian package · from Debian 12", "Built in"); Files as three radio rows
(File picker only, These folders with its folders as chips and Add folder,
All your files "never keys or passwords"; a Flatpak's rows below what its
package declares are insensitive); Devices, rows only for what it asked for
or used, the rest one "Other devices" row that opens in place; Network and
background (Network's "Using it now" in green); On screen, drawn by the
layer-permissions patch when it is in the build (a weak
cc_luma_view_on_screen_render), else nothing; Used recently, refusals
included; Remove (not for built-in apps), whose sheet (settings.html?page=remove) names the
documents found in its data folder by name and size in a well, with "Move them
to Documents" and "Keep its data" checked, Cancel then Remove in danger text: a
drawer with stacked 44 px actions on a phone, x1.5 with remote focus on Cancel
on a TV. While a running app takes a change only at its next start (a Flatpak),
Files ends with "<App> is open" and Restart <App> (settings.html?pending), which
asks AppPermissions1.RestartApp; the shell quits it the normal way and reopens it.

Apps gains "Apps that can use all your files" with the count, and its page
lists each app with origin and why and a switch; off is File picker only.

A fixture app may name its artwork beside the fixture (CFAPPINFO
spec_artwork), as 0109 does; the same hunk.

Settings carries the Lucide file-search and cable glyphs in its resources
(/org/gnome/Settings/icons) until the platform's icon set has them.
